  "market_context": "Gold was in a clear uptrend with sequential higher highs and higher lows, featuring distinct impulsive moves followed by corrective pullbacks. The analyst identified swing point A (low) and swing point B (high) of the latest impulse to define the retracement zone.",
  "key_observation": "In an established uptrend, price is highly likely to retest the 0.786 Fibonacci retracement level before breaking below swing low A and reversing the trend.",
  "analysis_steps": [
    "Step 1: Identify the most recent impulsive move from swing low A to swing high B in an obvious uptrend on the gold 1-hour chart.",
    "Step 2: Draw a Fibonacci retracement tool from A (low) to B (high) to locate key pullback levels.",
    "Step 3: Place a buy limit order precisely at the 0.786 Fibonacci level, as it represents a deep but high-probability trend continuation entry for assets like gold.",
    "Step 4: Set stop-loss a few pips below swing low A, and target swing high B to achieve approximately 1:3 risk-to-reward ratio."
  ],
  "outcome": null,
  "lessons": "The 0.786 Fibonacci level works best for trend continuation in assets with deep retracements like gold; confluence with market structure (higher highs/lows) increases reliability and R:R efficiency.",
